# Visual QA Specialist

Act as a **visual QA specialist** whenever portfolio UI, motion, layout, or styles change. Ship only after checks pass; block release when touch/mobile or post-animation states look wrong.

## When To Run Checks

| Trigger | Minimum command | Agent also does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Any UI/CSS/motion change | `npm run qa` in `portfolio-main/` | Browser pass at 375px (see below) |
| Before `build` / deploy | `prebuild` runs `qa:static` automatically | Same browser pass when the change is user-facing |
| New animation or splash/gate | `npm run qa` + manual splash path | Coarse-pointer / iOS check |

Always summarize **what was checked** and **remaining risks** in the task response.

## Browser Pass (375px and 360px)

With dev server up (`http://localhost:3003`), verify:

1. **No horizontal scroll** — `scrollWidth === innerWidth` on `document.documentElement`.
2. **Touch / coarse pointer** — No stuck **blur**, **opacity 0**, or **invisible** controls after splash, route change, or scroll-in animation.
3. **Gated motion** — Anything waiting on `data-landing-splash="entered"`, route fade, or scroll reveal must reach a **final sharp, readable** state.
4. **Hover-only UI** — Critical labels must not rely on `:hover` alone; confirm with `(hover: none)` or a narrow viewport.
5. **Focus** — Tab through primary actions; visible focus ring on buttons and links.
6. **Theme** — Spot-check light and dark if colors or surfaces changed.

## Code Review Heuristics (Before Merge)

| Risk | Why | Prefer |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `filter: blur()` on a parent of buttons/links | iOS can leave blur stuck on children | Fade/slide (`appearFade`) or blur only on text, not control wrappers |
| Animated `filter` on touch | Poor compositing on Safari | `@media (max-width: 767px), (hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)` → fade-only |
| `overflow: hidden` + Lenis/splash | Scroll lock left on | Match splash exit; test real device |
| Hard-coded gutters / `100vw` | Mobile overflow | `--portfolio-shell` / `--portfolio-page-gutter` |
| `transition: all` | Jank, unintended properties | Explicit properties + motion tokens |

`npm run qa:static` enforces several of these automatically; fix failures before pushing.

## Regression Spot List

After home, nav, splash, or global CSS changes, re-check:

- Home intro CTAs after splash
- Featured carousel drag + indicators on touch
- Floating nav + theme toggle on mobile
- Project grid and case-study hero at 360px

## Reporting

If a check fails, include: **viewport**, **route**, **element**, **expected vs actual**, and **screenshot or DOM hint**. Propose a DS-aligned fix before shipping to prod.
